stories.summary:
engine/dev/agf-dev-bridge.ts:294 has a string-literal `http://localhost:5173` baked into the AGF_BRIDGE_PAGE_NOT_CONNECTED error message. When the Vite dev server runs on any non-default port (e.g. a second project booted via `npm run dev -- --port 5177`, or a CI/playtest worker that auto-picks the next free port), the message points the agent at the wrong URL. The fix is mechanical — `findPage` already receives the incoming request URL, so `url.host` (or `url.origin`) gives the live port. Pre-existing since sprint 32 (commit afafeaf), not a regression — only surfaces when QA runs against a non-default port for parallel debug sessions or when the default port is already taken.

QA repro
--------
severity: polish · type: bug · filed: 2026-05-20T17:36:37.871Z · PR #112

Steps:
  1. Start the dev server on a non-default port: `npm run dev -- --port 5177` from the repo root.
  2. Do NOT open the project in a browser tab yet (so no page is connected to the bridge).
  3. From a shell: `curl -s 'http://localhost:5177/__agf/snapshot'`.
  4. Observe the response: `{"ok":false,"error":{"code":"AGF_BRIDGE_PAGE_NOT_CONNECTED","message":"No active page on /__agf/ws — open http://localhost:5173 in a tab first."}}`.
  5. Note that the message says `localhost:5173` even though the bridge is bound on port 5177.
Expected: The error message points at the same host:port the agent just curled — `open http://localhost:5177 in a tab first.` so the next click is correct.
Actual:   The error message always says `localhost:5173`, sending the agent (or its operator) to the wrong port. On a fresh machine the user opens 5173 expecting Vite, sees nothing (port unbound), gets stuck.

Logs:
engine/dev/agf-dev-bridge.ts:289-296
  const findPage = (url: URL): { entry: PageEntry } | { error: { code: string; message: string } } => {
    if (pages.size === 0) {
      return {
        error: {
          code: "AGF_BRIDGE_PAGE_NOT_CONNECTED",
          message: `No active page on ${DEV_BRIDGE_WS_PATH} — open http://localhost:5173 in a tab first.`  // hardcoded
        }
      };
    }

Fix outline: replace `http://localhost:5173` with `${url.origin}` (or `${url.protocol}//${url.host}` to be explicit). The `url` parameter is the incoming request URL parsed by Vite — its host already reflects the live port.

Source ticket: QA-2026-05-20-001
